sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-glue-15> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Temporary exposure of planarian fragments to a blocker of electrical synapses (gap junctions) causes them to build head shapes of other planarian species 100–150 million years distant, with no genetic change; Levin interprets this as the bioelectric network navigating to other attractors in morphospace, and the worms later remodel back to normal.";
    dc:type "experimental-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Transient gap-junction blockade makes planarian fragments build heads of other species";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Bioelectric networks: the cognitive glue enabling evolutionary scaling from physiology to mind”, Animal cognition (2023), doi:10.1007/s10071-023-01780-3; section “Basal cognition without neurons: what dynamic bodies think about › Creative problem-solving by adaptive morphogenesis: plasticity, not just emergent complexity”. Scope: Planarian flatworms (Girardia dorotocephala and related species), author's lab (Emmons-Bell et al. 2015)"
}
